{
  "cells": [
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "# Chunking Strategies for RAG Notebook\n\n> Hands-on Build It and Exercises."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Build It"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 1: fixed and recursive chunking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_fixed(text, size=512, overlap=0):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    step = size - overlap"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [text[i:i + size] for i in range(0, len(text), step)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_recursive(text, size=512, seps=(\"\\n\\n\", \"\\n\", \". \", \" \")):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if len(text) <= size:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [text]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for sep in seps:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if sep not in text:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        parts = text.split(sep)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        chunks = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        buf = \"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for p in parts:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if len(p) > size:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if buf:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    chunks.append(buf)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    buf = \"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                chunks.extend(chunk_recursive(p, size=size, seps=seps[1:] or (\" \",)))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                continue"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            candidate = buf + sep + p if buf else p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            if len(candidate) <= size:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                buf = candidate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                if buf:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                    chunks.append(buf)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "                buf = p"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if buf:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunks.append(buf)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return [c for c in chunks if c.strip()]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return chunk_fixed(text, size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 2: semantic chunking"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_semantic(text, encoder, threshold=0.6, min_chars=200, max_chars=2048):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    sentences = split_sentences(text)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    if not sentences:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        return []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    embs = encoder.encode(sentences, normalize_embeddings=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunks = [[sentences[0]]]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in range(1, len(sentences)):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        sim = float(embs[i] @ embs[i - 1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        current_len = sum(len(s) for s in chunks[-1])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if sim < threshold and current_len >= min_chars:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunks.append([sentences[i]])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            chunks[-1].append(sentences[i])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    result = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for group in chunks:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        text_group = \" \".join(group)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if len(text_group) > max_chars:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            result.extend(chunk_recursive(text_group, size=max_chars))"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        else:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            result.append(text_group)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return result"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Tune `threshold` on your domain. Too high \u2192 fragments. Too low \u2192 one giant chunk."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 3: parent-document"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def chunk_parent_child(text, parent_size=2048, child_size=256):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    parents = chunk_recursive(text, size=parent_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    mapping = []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for p_idx, parent in enumerate(parents):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        children = chunk_recursive(parent, size=child_size)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for child in children:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            mapping.append({\"child\": child, \"parent_idx\": p_idx, \"parent\": parent})"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return mapping"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        ""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def retrieve_parent(child_query, mapping, encoder, top_k=3):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    child_embs = encoder.encode([m[\"child\"] for m in mapping], normalize_embeddings=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    q_emb = encoder.encode([child_query], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    scores = child_embs @ q_emb"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    top = np.argsort(-scores)[:top_k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    seen, parents = set(), []"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for i in top:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if mapping[i][\"parent_idx\"] not in seen:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            parents.append(mapping[i][\"parent\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            seen.add(mapping[i][\"parent_idx\"])"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return parents"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Key insight: dedupe parents. Multiple children can map to the same parent; returning all would waste context."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 4: contextual retrieval (Anthropic pattern)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def contextualize_chunks(document, chunks, llm):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    context_prompts = ["
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        f\"\"\"<document>{document}</document>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Here is the chunk to situate: <chunk>{c}</chunk>"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Write 50-100 words placing this chunk in the document's context.\"\"\""
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        for c in chunks"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    ]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    contexts = llm.batch(context_prompts)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return [f\"{ctx}\\n\\n{c}\" for ctx, c in zip(contexts, chunks)]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Index the contextualized chunks. At query time, retrieval benefits from the extra surrounding signal."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "### Step 5: evaluate"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```python"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "def recall_at_k(queries, corpus_chunks, encoder, k=5):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    chunk_embs = encoder.encode(corpus_chunks, normalize_embeddings=True)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    hits = 0"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    for q_text, gold_idxs in queries:"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        q_emb = encoder.encode([q_text], normalize_embeddings=True)[0]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        top = np.argsort(-(chunk_embs @ q_emb))[:k]"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "        if any(i in gold_idxs for i in top):"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "            hits += 1"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "    return hits / len(queries)"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "```"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "Always benchmark. The \"best\" strategy for your corpus may not match any blog post."
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "markdown",
      "source": [
        "## Exercises"
      ]
    },
    {
      "cell_type": "code",
      "source": [
        "1. **Easy.** Chunk one 20-page document with fixed(512, 0), recursive(512, 0), and recursive(512, 100). Compare chunk counts and boundary quality.\n2. **Medium.** Build a 30-query eval set over 5 documents. Measure recall@5 for recursive, semantic, and parent-document. Which wins? Does it match the blog posts?\n3. **Hard.** Implement contextual retrieval. Measure MRR improvement over baseline recursive. Report index cost (LLM calls) vs accuracy gain."
      ]
    }
